nces cited in the text provide evidence and studies related to dumping syndrome and its management.", "DIAZÓXIDO:", "PERREAULT L.:Perreault L. es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre la terapia dietética para la obesidad en adultos.", "KUNINS L.:Kunins L. es un editor que ha colaborado en la obra de UpToDate sobre la obesidad en adultos.", "BMI:BMI, or Body Mass Index, is a widely used measure that assesses an individual's body weight in relation to their height. This calculation helps categorize individuals into different classifications: underweight, normal weight, overweight, or obese. BMI serves as an important tool in evaluating nutritional status and can influence the nutritional support needs of patients. It is commonly utilized in obesity and health assessments to provide insights into an individual's weight status, thereby aiding in the identification of potential health risks associated with being underweight or overweight.", "LOW-FAT DIET:A low-fat diet is a dietary plan that restricts fat intake, often used for weight loss and health improvement.", "LOW-CARBOHYDRATE DIET:A low-carbohydrate diet is a dietary plan that limits carbohydrate intake, aimed at weight loss and managing blood sugar levels.", "BARIATRIC SURGERY:Bariatric surgery is a medical procedure designed for weight loss through various surgical techniques that modify the digestive system. This includes methods such as gastrectomy and bypass surgery. It is primarily recommended for individuals suffering from obesity and related health issues, including Type 2 diabetes, as it aims to achieve significant weight loss and improve metabolic health. \n\nThe procedure is recognized as the most effective treatment for patients with morbid obesity, leading to various physiological changes, including hormonal alterations and modifications in intestinal microbiota that contribute to weight loss. However, bariatric surgery also necessitates specific dietary adjustments post-operation and is 